"dan-fouts": [
  "Football is a game of confidence, and that confidence is built by meticulous preparation and relentless practice.",
  "When you run the Air Coryell offense, you don't just test the defense vertically; you use the entire field and force them to cover every blade of grass.",
  "We didn't have room for divas in our offense; every single receiver had to run hard on every route because the coverage dictated where the ball went.",
  "You strive to win a Super Bowl and you do everything humanly possible to get there, but being enshrined in the Hall of Fame is an honor you never even dare to play for.",
  "Don Coryell completely revolutionized how football is played, pushing the game forward and forcing defenses to invent nickel and dime packages just to survive.",
  "As a quarterback, your job is to stand tall in the pocket, take the hits, and deliver the ball downfield with absolute precision.",
  "You learn early on that leadership isn't about being loud in the locker room; it's about executing your reads when the pressure is at its absolute peak.",
  "Playing through the elements, whether it's freezing cold in Buffalo or a grueling shootout in San Diego, is what separates a professional from a passenger.",
  "Preparation during the week in the film room is what allows the game to slow down on Sunday afternoon so you can pick apart a complex zone coverage.",
  "You have to have a short memory for interceptions; if you hesitate for even a fraction of a second, you can't play this position at a high level.",
  "The trust between a quarterback and his targets is forged through thousands of reps in the scorching summer heat when nobody else is watching.",
  "We wanted to attack you from every angle, putting maximum stress on the secondary until they broke.",
  "You respect every defensive coordinator trying to confuse you with disguises, but you trust your eyes and your arm above everything else.",
  "The bonds and shared battles with your offensive linemen—the guys who sacrificed their bodies to keep you upright—are what you cherish most when your career is over.",
  "When the game is on the line in the fourth quarter, that is the exact moment you dream about as a kid throwing passes in the backyard.",
  "At the end of the day, your legacy is built on whether you changed the way the game was played and left everything you had on the turf."
],
