  "Preparation during the week under Coryell's Air Coryell system meant running deep seams until your lungs burned, just so you could outrun safeties who thought they had angle on you.",
  "You don't lead the NFL in receptions twice as a tight end without catching everything within a five-mile radius and refusing to let linebackers intimidate you.",
